WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.739
Learn to find the simplest form of given fractions by dividing through by the highest

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:10.170
common factor (i.e. by cancelling through by factors) and recognise fractions that

00:00:10.170 --> 00:00:14.971
are greater than one (i.e. improper fractions), draw and label such fractions with

00:00:14.971 --> 00:00:15.709
their symbols

00:00:16.533 --> 00:00:24.119
Simplify 42/84 to lowest terms. The answer is 1/2. Divide by 7 and simplify any other

00:00:24.119 --> 00:00:25.067
common factor.

00:00:25.867 --> 00:00:31.465
A shaded diagram shows 18 out of 21 equal squares. What is this fraction in lowest

00:00:31.465 --> 00:00:34.613
terms? Pause and solve it in your exercise book.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:40.890
The answer is 6/7. Divide numerator and denominator by their common factor.
